# Which country emits the most CO₂ per person?
subtitle: "Pick the country that emits the most CO₂ per person from five oil and gas states, then see how a year in Congo compares with half a day there."
tags: ["earth","geography","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Not the one you think\" note \"CO₂ per person\""

## Which country emits the most CO₂ per person?
text: {"font_size":34}
sources:
    - id: owid_pc
      title: CO₂ emissions per capita
      authors: Our World in Data, from the Global Carbon Budget (2025)
      year: 2025
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/co-emissions-per-capita
      finding: 'in 2024, tonnes of CO₂ per person: Qatar 41.3, Kuwait 26.2, Trinidad and Tobago 22.9, Saudi Arabia 20.4, United Arab Emirates 20.1, United States 14.2, world 4.7, Democratic Republic of Congo 0.054; nine countries are above the US (Qatar, Kuwait, Brunei, Bahrain, Trinidad and Tobago, Saudi Arabia, UAE, Oman, Australia)'

