    card title "Most CO₂ per person?"

A: Forty-one tonnes of carbon dioxide, every year, for every person. That's the world record. Which country holds it?
    draw big41 big41s

B: Let me guess: America. Big cars, big houses, big everything.
    icon usa_g size 140 set twemoji x 500 y 290 icon_look picture of "flag united states"
    text usa_q "?" #8f887c x 610 y 290 font_size 90

    erase big41 big41s usa_g usa_q

A: Not even close. Nine countries beat America. Here are five of them.
    draw row

    ask "Tap the flag you think it is." choose ["fl_kwt","fl_qat","fl_sau","fl_tto","fl_are"] answer fl_qat store c
        right: It's Qatar, at about forty-one tonnes a person in 2024.
        wrong: A hint: this country hosted the 2022 football World Cup.

A: The others sit between twenty and twenty-six tonnes. An American: fourteen. The world average: about five.
    draw bars ln0 lt0 ln1 lt1

B: So the common thread is oil and gas, with very few people to share the bill.
    draw w_gas

A: Right: emissions count where the gas is produced, even when it's exported. Then add air conditioning, and seawater made drinkable.
    draw w_ac w_water

    erase row bars ln0 lt0 ln1 lt1 w_gas w_ac w_water

B: Here's the comparison that got me. A person in the Democratic Republic of the Congo emits about fifty kilos a year.
    draw p_c pf_c ic_c kg50

A: And someone in Qatar passes fifty kilos in less than half a day.
    draw p_q pf_q eq ic_q half

B: Half a day there, a whole year here. Same sky, same air.
    highlight half

